   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The integrand is a product of x and an exponential, and the derivative of the exponent, \\( -3 \\), does not account for the factor x, so substitution does not apply and the product calls for integration by parts.",
         "rule_named": "technique selected by structure"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Take \\( u = 5 x \\) and \\( dv = e^{- 3 x}\\,dx \\), so \\( du = 5\\,dx \\) and \\( v = - \\frac{e^{- 3 x}}{3} \\). Then the integral is \\( - \\frac{5 x e^{- 3 x}}{3} + \\int \\frac{5 e^{- 3 x}}{3}\\,dx \\).",
         "rule_named": "integration by parts"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Antidifferentiate the remaining exponential: the integral is \\( - \\frac{5 x e^{- 3 x}}{3} - \\frac{5 e^{- 3 x}}{9} + C \\).",
